{"id": "EUVD-2026-103548", "enisaUuid": "287ceef1-6889-307c-bba9-1984c8dbc5d1", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nscsi: sd_zbc: Reject disks with too many zones\n\nsd_zbc_read_zones() computes the number of zones with 64-bit arithmetic and\nstores the result in the unsigned int nr_zones field of struct\nzoned_disk_info, silently truncating counts that exceed 32 bits. The\ntruncated count is later used to size per-zone resources, while the device\nmay still report more zones than fit.\n\nMoreover, sd_zbc_report_zones() counts the reported zones with a signed int\nzone_idx, which overflows past INT_MAX. Reject devices reporting more than\nINT_MAX zones at scan time; such a device is not realistic for any medium\nthat exists today, and accepting it produces inconsistent zone bookkeeping.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:20:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:23:03", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d8791ae55d85dfaeafa20ea48365482a0cc5a107", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0af16d8be3ec7ff28bb56a0da79c9aed66ac2c3b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3ddf8383b54456f19fd73d3cebed81bd250c7388", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6ec0f79745967c751c85df373062c8d15e45fc4"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gc5v-q6x9-gww4", "CVE-2026-98634"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02d98160-3f08-33fd-84d6-0b9e98803a04", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89d9475610771b5e5fe1879075f0fc9ba6e3755f <d8791ae55d85dfaeafa20ea48365482a0cc5a107"}, {"id": "373a8a06-45c6-3531-9198-5b5ceb9842ff", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "38797f14-2929-36ff-8c00-539379bd3392", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.10"}, {"id": "69d5cc2f-c67b-3716-9c25-88c4071e8228", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89d9475610771b5e5fe1879075f0fc9ba6e3755f <b6ec0f79745967c751c85df373062c8d15e45fc4"}, {"id": "883b3258-9558-3153-9574-cb5c6ed5b11f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89d9475610771b5e5fe1879075f0fc9ba6e3755f <3ddf8383b54456f19fd73d3cebed81bd250c7388"}, {"id": "d46b26f5-a644-3d34-98a7-8839ce833164", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "d56f44dd-bfd2-3144-8d2c-8ea3f846f864", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "d94186d9-76b9-396a-a64d-1119832014e1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "d9584c32-cb6c-32ad-951a-5de1c2987f7d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "eeec5c99-0d40-333d-94f3-f082bdbc6342", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "89d9475610771b5e5fe1879075f0fc9ba6e3755f <0af16d8be3ec7ff28bb56a0da79c9aed66ac2c3b"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "cfa9ac79-9ca7-3fac-b06b-066865af7279", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}